WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Treasure Island

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.200
Come, mates!
To the treasure!

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:24.860
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest...

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:29.420
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum!

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:32.430
<i>This is it, the race to
the treasure has started.</i>

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.670
<i>Will it belong to Silver?</i>

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:36.140
<i>Or to us?</i>

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.920
Treasure
Island

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.720
Takarajima

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.530
saa ikou

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.530
Come, let's go

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.620
yume ni mita shima heto

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.620
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:01.460
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:01.460
Across the waves, on the wind

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:04.340
umi hedeyou

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:04.340
We'll travel the oceans

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.260
ikute ni wa

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.260
Many of us

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:10.260
minna mada shiranai

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:10.260
Still don't know of

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:14.010
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:14.010
The days and nights full of mystery

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.510
matte iru darou

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.510
That await us there

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.020
itsumo shinji you

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.020
We must always have trust

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.270
magokoro wo

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.270
And be sincere

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:29.530
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:29.530
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.660
tade hitotsu no

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.660
I only...

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:36.080
akogare dake wa

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:36.080
...have one desire

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:38.370
doko no dare ni mo

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:38.370
And no one...

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:45.080
kese wa shinai sa

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:45.080
...will ever take it away

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.630
tade hitotsu no

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.630
I only...

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.930
akogare dake wa

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:54.930
...have one desire

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.260
doko no dare ni mo

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.260
And no one...

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:04.190
kese wa shinai sa

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:04.190
...will ever take it away

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:15.150
episode

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:15.150
A Treasure is Good
\h  Only If You're Alive!

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.980
"Face North-Northeast and a quarter North."

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:27.120
"...foothills of the Spyglass.
Big tree..."

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.290
"Skeleton Island, East Southeast and a quarter East."

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.250
We still can't see Skeleton Island.

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:38.720
Everyone, get up!
The treasure is still far off!

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.250
What a complete and utter idiot!

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:46.640
That map isn't going to help him find the treasure.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:50.600
I don't think he'll discover the hidden paragraphs,

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:56.070
but when he finds nothing there,
I fear he'll harm Jim.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:57.820
Don't worry.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:03.200
We'll arrange to take back Jim before Silver reaches the fake hiding place.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.130
They're on the move again!

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:28.270
So you want to take back Jim before they reach the fake hiding place.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:32.460
But, are we really sure...

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.570
...that it's a false trail?

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.780
What do you mean, Livesey?

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.940
What if the map that we gave them,

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.660
indicates the real location of the treasure?

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.900
That's nonsense, Livesey!

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:48.220
What about the paragraphs in invisible ink?

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:51.060
Undeniably, we witnessed these mysterious notes.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:54.280
After that, we immediately concluded...

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:58.980
...that these lines indicated the true location of the treasure.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:03.460
But the key to this puzzle still eludes us.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:07.030
Nothing says that they are related to the treasure.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:11.640
N-Not related to the treasure?
L-Livesey...

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.480
S-So you mean...

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:17.380
...that the copy we made is no use to us?

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:19.180
Wait, I didn't say that.

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:21.110
It's only a possibility.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:28.330
Who goes there?!

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:33.000
Who are you?
Show yourself!

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:37.170
D-Did Silver send a man to spy on us?

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:40.510
Ho!
Wait, don't shoot!

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:44.050
I'm not one of them.
I'm a friend of Jim!

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:45.430
Of Jim?

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:48.640
I see, then you must be Mr. Ben Gunn!

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.560
That's right.
Nice to meet you, gents.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:55.660
Hey Flint, go motivate them a bit.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:56.630
Okay.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.190
Too slow, too slow!
Hurry up, hurry up!

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:03.150
Too slow, too slow!
Hurry up, hurry up!

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.120
The foothills of the Spyglass...

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.700
Face North-Northeast and a quarter North.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:17.120
Pay attention to where you put your feet!

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.670
The rock is frail!

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.600
Fifteen men...

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:29.520
...on a dead man's chest!

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:35.770
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum!

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:39.380
Drink and the devil...

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:44.490
...had done for the rest!

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:49.330
Yo-ho-ho!
...and another bottle of rum!

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:02.250
Clumsy ol' me...

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:12.430
Don't give up, Giraffe!
The treasure is waiting!

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:21.810
Hey, you can go.
I'll watch him.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:37.580
Anderson, your fever'll go down when you see the treasure. Stay strong!

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:40.040
Y-Yes, boss...

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:46.960
Tattoo! Just think of what you're going to do with your share of the loot.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:50.930
Monkey-Face!
Think of the gold coins!

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:09.650
Hey, George and Morgan,

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:13.370
the next time you want to betray me,
do it after we've found the treasure.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:15.990
That might provide you with better results.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:19.960
However, be prepared to put your life on the line.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:25.150
That's it, George.
That's the attitude.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:31.260
Moron, idiot, slug, slowpoke!

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:34.380
Wet-pants, lazy, laggard!

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:38.360
Cut me some slack...
You're very hard on me.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:42.980
I'm exhausted.
I can't go on, geez!

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:46.940
Hey, Puppy! You can kiss your share goodbye if you stop here!

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:50.860
Anything... but that!

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.260
Have mercy!

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:52.960
Mercy!

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:11.260
It's going to be dark soon.
They'll camp over there.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:15.230
And tomorrow, they'll arrive at the spot indicated on the map.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:19.720
We'll take back Jim tonight.
We'll strike while they're asleep.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:36.490
Someone's fallen.

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:39.880
My God...
It's not Jim, is it?

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:42.460
No, Jim's alright.
He's with Silver.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:48.540
S-Silver, you're not going to help him?

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:52.200
If he survives, he'll come back to us.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:55.340
As it stands, we have no use for men who can't take care of themselves.

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:20.030
You sure you'll be okay by yourself, Gray?

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:22.540
Yes, I prefer it that way.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:25.790
Should I fail, we won't lose an extra soul.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.260
Has Gray left?

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:35.800
Yes.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:38.090
Gray, bring us Jim!

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:57.330
Look at that, Flint.

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:01.780
It's not often that we have a nightly visitor.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:22.760
Sorry, Gray, but I still need Jim.

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:26.500
Don't worry. I promise nothing's going to happen to him.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:28.020
Tell that to the others.

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:32.080
As you wish.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:35.400
I've always wanted to see that famous knife skill of yours.

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:51.420
Not bad, I complement you for keeping up so far.

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:54.380
But you lack a bit of experience...

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:59.130
Don't worry, I'll help gain what you lack.
You'll catch up before you know it.

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:07.850
He's a force to be reckoned with....

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:22.830
What is it, Jim?
Did you dream about the treasure?

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:27.450
You'll see it tomorrow.
Not in your dreams, but the real thing.

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:01.730
East-Southeast and a quarter East,
Skeleton Island.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:07.760
Face North-Northeast and a quarter North.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:11.230
The foothills of the Spyglass.
A big tree...

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:21.420
Jim, I still cannot believe that he has only one leg.

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:23.970
Even on these steep hills,

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:27.400
he's very far ahead of us.

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:31.350
It must be because we're moving towards the treasure.

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:34.310
It's almost as if he has two legs.

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:41.240
He's obsessed, I bet.

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:42.610
Obsessed?

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:43.200
Yep.

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:45.720
He's obsessed with the treasure.

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:48.030
I don't see any other explanation.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:08.520
Face North-Northeast and a quarter North.

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:11.220
The foothills of the Spyglass.

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:14.520
And a big tree...

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:28.070
<i>You've done it, Silver!</i>

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:06.540
<i>"J.F."</i>

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:09.450
<i>No doubt about it.
These are Flint's initials!</i>

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:12.570
It's here!

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:17.570
I've found it!
At last!

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:37.160
What's up with you?
Don't just stand there gaping!

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:38.480
Snap out of it!

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:44.230
Bring this treasure, that has slept beneath the earth for so long, to the light of day!

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:46.440
Let's go!
Our treasure is there!

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:49.490
Don't be shy!
Hurry and dig it up!

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:58.870
Let's get it out of there!

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:02.130
All the treasure!

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:31.660
Why do you make that face, Jim?

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:34.660
Come on, I want to see you smile.

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:37.580
Do it for me.
Okay?

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:40.480
According to Puppy,

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:42.790
you're obsessed with the treasure.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:49.200
You walked faster than everyone else...

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:52.070
As if my leg had re-grown, you mean?

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:57.720
Listen, Jim. When a man
decides to do something,

00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:01.620
whether he has one, two or even
three legs—doesn't mean anything.

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:05.640
When I've set my mind to something,
I always see it through to the end.

00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:07.660
Be it right or wrong.

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:09.620
That is my philosophy.

00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:42.430
I-I want to dig, too!
Let me dig!

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:52.700
Hey, Anderson.
Don't be stupid!

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:54.700
You're in no shape to dig.

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.660
Don't stop him.
Let him dig.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:03.120
Anderson is an old friend of mine.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.250
Let him do as he pleases!

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:30.070
We've found the treasure!

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:56.050
We better not.

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:58.200
There isn't the smallest rock to take cover behind.

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:01.160
We can't get close enough to save Jim like this.

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:06.120
Mr. Ben Gunn, is there a way
we can get closer under cover?

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:07.600
You must know some way.

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:10.000
I'm afraid I do not.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:13.570
I almost never come here because there's nothing to eat.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:26.760
If one of us dies, our share will increase.

00:18:26.760 --> 00:18:30.000
If two of us die, it will increase even more.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:34.240
If three of us die, we'll have one hundred more gold pieces.

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:38.480
With four deaths, there will be two hundred more gold pieces.

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:42.360
With five deaths, a large diamond.

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:45.480
If we all die, who will get it?

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:49.560
Who will the treasure go to?

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:51.440
Idiot!

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:55.730
It's useless to even consider that!

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:58.700
A treasure is only useful if you're alive.

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:01.830
Let's do this!

00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:16.910
There it is!
The dead don't need it.

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:45.410
I'll open it.

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:27.280
Wh-What does this mean?!

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:32.590
There isn't any treasure...
Just a single skull.

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:41.170
<i>As I thought, Mr. Trelawney was right.</i>

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:45.140
<i>The true location is written in invisible ink.</i>

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:49.680
Of course, that must be it.

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:50.770
They beat us to it.

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:54.080
They've already dug up the treasure...

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:56.320
...and hidden it somewhere.

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.450
That's why they let us have the map.

00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:01.660
Aint that right, kid?!

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:04.950
Yes, when you think about it...

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:07.520
I see, you've tricked us!

00:21:07.520 --> 00:21:10.120
Darn, brat!
Talk or you'll regret it!

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:16.540
Don't let him escape!

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:41.190
My God!
They've tied up Jim!

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:49.880
Wh-What do you want?
What are you doing?!

00:21:49.880 --> 00:21:54.250
Isn't that obvious? We're going to make you cough up the treasure!

00:21:58.680 --> 00:22:00.270
Do you still not understand?!

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:04.270
I won't let anyone touch the kid.

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:09.590
The chest is empty and you aren't the only ones who are angry!

00:22:10.360 --> 00:22:14.160
I, too, am angry.

00:22:14.160 --> 00:22:17.560
So you better not annoy me.

00:22:28.390 --> 00:22:32.280
To      be        continued

00:22:33.520 --> 00:22:38.560
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:33.520 --> 00:22:38.560
Hey sea breeze

00:22:38.560 --> 00:22:44.370
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:38.560 --> 00:22:44.370
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:45.590 --> 00:22:50.580
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:45.590 --> 00:22:50.580
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:50.580 --> 00:22:56.020
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:50.580 --> 00:22:56.020
A word to my dear mother

00:22:56.020 --> 00:23:01.430
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:56.020 --> 00:23:01.430
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:01.430 --> 00:23:06.890
kaban ippai no

00:23:01.430 --> 00:23:06.890
And that my bag filled

00:23:06.890 --> 00:23:12.520
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:06.890 --> 00:23:12.520
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:12.520 --> 00:23:18.380
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:12.520 --> 00:23:18.380
Will be brought back

00:23:19.470 --> 00:23:24.970
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:19.470 --> 00:23:24.970
The sunset on my back

00:23:24.970 --> 00:23:30.860
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:24.970 --> 00:23:30.860
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:30.860 --> 00:23:40.580
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:30.860 --> 00:23:40.580
I blow out a whistle

00:23:45.260 --> 00:23:46.980
The treasure wasn't there.

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:49.950
The pirates complain more and more.

00:23:49.950 --> 00:23:52.640
The way this is heading,
they may revolt again.

00:23:52.640 --> 00:23:53.830
Silver and I are in danger.

00:23:54.340 --> 00:24:00.130
Along with the tension, the chest's skull remains silent as if it's taunting us.

00:24:00.130 --> 00:24:03.100
Suddenly, a spark ignites in Silver's eyes.

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:06.480
Next time on Treasure Island:
"When a Pirates Dies, He Leaves Only a Skeleton"

00:24:06.480 --> 00:24:09.360
The dead are silent,
but their corpses speak.

00:24:08.590 --> 00:24:13.590
m 0 0 l 960 0 960 720 0 720

00:24:08.590 --> 00:24:13.590
*

00:24:08.590 --> 00:24:13.590
Next time

00:24:08.590 --> 00:24:13.590
Coming soon!

00:24:08.590 --> 00:24:13.590
When A Pirate Dies,
He Leaves Only A Skeleton
